  "output": "# Performance Analysis - CarabinerOS Frontend\n\n## 🔴 Critical Issues\n\n### 1. **Unbounded Memory Growth in Hooks**\n\n**Location:** `use-action-cards.ts`, `use-chat.ts`\n\n**Problem:** The `processedIds` Sets grow indefinitely and are never cleared.\n\n```typescript\n// Current (MEMORY LEAK)\nconst processedIds = useRef(new Set<string>());\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  for (const log of snapshot.logs) {\n    if (processedIds.current.has(log.id)) continue;\n    // ... process log\n    processedIds.current.add(log.id); // ❌ Never removed\n  }\n}, [snapshot]);\n```\n\n**Fix:** Implement LRU cache with size limit or clear old entries:\n\n```typescript\nconst processedIds = useRef(new Set<string>());\nconst MAX_PROCESSED_IDS = 1000;\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (!snapshot) return;\n  \n  const newCards: ActionCard[] = [];\n  \n  for (const log of snapshot.logs) {\n    const logKey = log.id;\n    if (processedIds.current.has(logKey)) continue;\n    \n    if (log.type === \"tool\" && log.kvps?.module && log.kvps?.action) {\n      newCards.push({\n        id: log.id,\n        type: String(log.kvps.action),\n        module: String(log.kvps.module),\n        // ... rest of card\n      });\n      processedIds.current.add(logKey);\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Batch state update instead of individual updates\n  if (newCards.length > 0) {\n    setCards(prev => [...prev, ...newCards]);\n  }\n  \n  // Prevent unbounded growth\n  if (processedIds.current.size > MAX_PROCESSED_IDS) {\n    const arr = Array.from(processedIds.current);\n    processedIds.current = new Set(arr.slice(-MAX_PROCESSED_IDS));\n  }\n}, [snapshot]);\n```\n\n**Impact:** 🔥 **High** - Memory leak in long-running sessions\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Inefficient State Updates in Loops**\n\n**Location:** `use-action-cards.ts:26-40`\n\n**Problem:** Calling `setCards` inside a loop causes multiple re-renders.\n\n```typescript\n// Current (BAD - multiple renders)\nfor (const log of snapshot.logs) {\n  // ...\n  setCards(prev => [...prev, card]); // ❌ Re-render on each iteration\n  processedIds.current.add(log.id);\n}\n```\n\n**Fix:** Batch updates (shown in fix above).\n\n**Impact:** 🔥 **High** - Causes N re-renders instead of 1\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Missing Cleanup for Timeouts**\n\n**Location:** `use-expo-stream.ts:99-108`, `use-expo-stream.ts:111-120`\n\n**Problem:** Timeouts not cleaned up if `chefStatus` or `snapshot` change rapidly.\n\n```typescript\n// Current (MEMORY LEAK)\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (!chefStatus?.active) {\n    setExpo({ text: chefStatus.text, thoughts: [], active: false });\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n      setExpo(prev => \n        prev.active ? prev : { text: null, thoughts: [], active: false }\n      );\n    }, 3000);\n    // ❌ No cleanup!\n  }\n}, [chefStatus]);\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```typescript\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (!chefStatus) return;\n\n  if (!chefStatus.active) {\n    stickyTextRef.current = null;\n    setExpo({ text: chefStatus.text, thoughts: [], active: false });\n    \n    const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n      setExpo(prev =>\n        prev.active ? prev : { text: null, thoughts: [], active: false }\n      );\n    }, 3000);\n    \n    return () => clearTimeout(timer); // ✅ Cleanup\n  }\n}, [chefStatus]);\n```\n\n**Impact:** 🔥 **High** - Stale closures and potential state corruption\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 Performance Optimizations\n\n### 4. **Redundant Motion Variants Creation**\n\n**Location:** Multiple workspace pages (food-cost, inventory, marketing, menu, orders)\n\n**Problem:** Motion variants recreated on every render.\n\n```typescript\n// Current (BAD - new object every render)\nconst cardVariants = {\n  hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 12 },\n  visible: (i: number) => ({\n    opacity: 1, y: 0,\n    transition: { delay: i * 0.08, duration: 0.35 }\n  }),\n};\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return <motion.div variants={cardVariants} />; // ❌\n}\n```\n\n**Fix:** Move outside component or memoize:\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ Define outside component\nconst cardVariants: Variants = {\n  hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 12 },\n  visible: (i: number) => ({\n    opacity: 1,\n    y: 0,\n    transition: { delay: i * 0.08, duration: 0.35, ease: [0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94] }\n  }),\n};\n\n// Or use useMemo for dynamic values\nconst cardVariants = useMemo(() => ({\n  hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 12 },\n  // ...\n}), []); // Empty deps if truly static\n```\n\n**Impact:** 🟡 **Medium** - Unnecessary object allocations on every render\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Missing React.memo on Expensive Components**\n\n**Location:** Workspace table rows, KPI cards\n\n**Problem:** Child components re-render even when props haven't changed.\n\n```typescript\n// Current\nfunction KpiCard({ label, value, icon: Icon, accent, bar, delay }: KpiCardProps) {\n  return (\n    <motion.div>\n      {/* ... */}\n    </motion.div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```typescript\nconst KpiCard = React.memo(function KpiCard({ \n  label, value, icon: Icon, accent, bar, delay \n}: KpiCardProps) {\n  return (\n    <motion.div\n      initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 16 }}\n      animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}\n      transition={{ duration: 0.4, delay, ease: EASE }}\n      className=\"relative overflow-hidden rounded-xl border bg-card p-5\"\n    >\n      {/* ... */}\n    </motion.div>\n  );\n});\n```\n\nApply to: `KpiCard`, `PressureBadge`, `VarianceBar`, `PipelineStrip`, etc.\n\n**Impact:** 🟡 **Medium** - Reduces re-renders in workspace pages\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Redundant Parsing in Table Renders**\n\n**Location:** All workspace pages with tables\n\n**Problem:** Parse functions called on every render for every row.\n\n```typescript\n// Current (BAD)\n<TableCell>{formatCurrency(order.total)}</TableCell>\n<TableCell>{formatDate(order.created_at)}</TableCell>\n```\n\n**Fix:** Memoize parsed data:\n\n```typescript\nconst processedOrders = useMemo(() => \n  filteredOrders.map(order => ({\n    ...order,\n    totalFormatted: formatCurrency(order.total),\n    dateFormatted: formatDate(order.created_at),\n  })),\n  [filteredOrders]\n);\n\n// In render\n<TableCell>{order.totalFormatted}</TableCell>\n<TableCell>{order.dateFormatted}</TableCell>\n```\n\n**Impact:** 🟡 **Medium** - O(n) computation saved on every render\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Socket Event Listener Leak**\n\n**Location:** `use-socket.ts:32-55`\n\n**Problem:** Multiple effect cleanups could race.\n\n```typescript\n// Current\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const socket = initStateSyncSocket();\n  \n  socket.on(\"connect\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  socket.on(\"disconnect\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  socket.on(\"state_push\", (envelope) => { /* ... */ });\n  socket.on(\"chef_status\", (status) => { /* ... */ });\n  \n  getCsrfToken()\n    .then(() => socket.connect())\n    .catch(() => socket.connect());\n\n  return () => {\n    socket.off(\"connect\");\n    socket.off(\"disconnect\");\n    socket.off(\"state_push\");\n    socket.off(\"chef_status\");\n    socket.disconnect();\n  };\n}, []); // ✅ Good - empty deps\n```\n\n**Fix:** Store handlers in refs to ensure exact same function is removed:\n\n```typescript\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const socket = initStateSyncSocket();\n  socketRef.current = socket;\n\n  const handleConnect = () => {\n    setConnected(true);\n    socket.emit(\"state_request\", {\n      context: null,\n      log_from: 0,\n      // ...\n    });\n  };\n\n  const handleDisconnect = () => setConnected(false);\n  \n  const handleStatePush = (envelope: A0StatePush) => {\n    // ...\n  };\n  \n  const handleChefStatus = (status: ChefStatus) => {\n    setChefStatus(status);\n  };\n\n  socket.on(\"connect\", handleConnect);\n  socket.on(\"disconnect\", handleDisconnect);\n  socket.on(\"state_push\", handleStatePush);\n  socket.on(\"chef_status\", handleChefStatus);\n\n  getCsrfToken()\n    .then(() => socket.connect())\n    .catch(() => socket.connect());\n\n  return () => {\n    socket.off(\"connect\", handleConnect);\n    socket.off(\"disconnect\", handleDisconnect);\n    socket.off(\"state_push\", handleStatePush);\n    socket.off(\"chef_status\", handleChefStatus);\n    socket.disconnect();\n  };\n}, []);\n```\n\n**Impact:** 🟡 **Medium** - Prevents duplicate listeners\n\n---\n\n## 🟢 Nice-to-Have Optimizations\n\n### 8. **Add Request Deduplication & Caching**\n\n**Location:** `use-workspace.ts`\n\n**Problem:** Every mount triggers a fresh fetch, no deduplication.\n\n**Fix:** Use SWR or React Query:\n\n```typescript\nimport useSWR from 'swr';\n\nconst fetcher = (url: string) => \n  fetch(url, { credentials: \"include\" }).then(res => {\n    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`${res.status}`);\n    return res.json();\n  });\n\nexport function useWorkspace<T = Record<string, unknown>>(\n  endpoint: string,\n  locationId?: string,\n): UseWorkspaceReturn<T> {\n  const url = locationId\n    ? `${endpoint}?location_id=${locationId}`\n    : endpoint;\n\n  const { data, error, isLoading, mutate } = useSWR<{\n    items?: T[];\n    data?: T[];\n  }>(url, fetcher, {\n    revalidateOnFocus: false,\n    dedupingInterval: 2000, // Dedupe requests within 2s\n  });\n\n  const items = Array.isArray(data) \n    ? data \n    : data?.items ?? data?.data ?? [];\n\n  return {\n    data: items as T[],\n    loading: isLoading,\n    error: error?.message ?? null,\n    refresh: mutate,\n  };\n}\n```\n\n**Impact:** 🟢 **Low-Medium** - Better UX, reduced server load\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Virtualize Long Lists**\n\n**Location:** Workspace tables with 100+ items\n\n**Fix:** Use `@tanstack/react-virtual`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual';\n\nfunction VirtualizedTable({ items }: { items: Order[] }) {\n  const parentRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n\n  const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n    count: items.length,\n    getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n    estimateSize: () => 60, // Row height in px\n    overscan: 5,\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div ref={parentRef} style={{ height: '600px', overflow: 'auto' }}>\n      <div style={{ height: `${virtualizer.getTotalSize()}px`, position: 'relative' }}>\n        {virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map(virtualRow => {\n          const item = items[virtualRow.index];\n          return (\n            <div\n              key={item.id}\n              style={{\n                position: 'absolute',\n                top: 0,\n                left: 0,\n                width: '100%',\n                height: `${virtualRow.size}px`,\n                transform: `translateY(${virtualRow.start}px)`,\n              }}\n            >\n              {/* Row content */}\n            </div>\n          );\n        })}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Impact:** 🟢 **Low** (unless 500+ items) - Massive improvement for large datasets\n\n---\n\n### 10. **Debounce Search Input**\n\n**Location:** Workspace pages with search\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { useDeferredValue } from 'react';\n\nfunction WorkspacePage() {\n  const [searchInput, setSearchInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const deferredSearch = useDeferredValue(searchInput);\n  \n  const filtered = useMemo(() => \n    data.filter(item => \n      item.name.toLowerCase().includes(deferredSearch.toLowerCase())\n    ),\n    [data, deferredSearch] // Uses deferred value\n  );\n\n  return (\n    <Input\n      value={searchInput} // Controlled with immediate value\n      onChange={(e) => setSearchInput(e.target.value)}\n      placeholder=\"Search...\"\n    />\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Impact:** 🟢 **Low** - Smoother typing experience\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Issue | Severity | Impact | Effort | Priority |\n|-------|----------|--------|--------|----------|\n| Unbounded Set growth | 🔴 Critical | Memory leak | Low | **P0** |\n| State updates in loops | 🔴 Critical | N renders | Low | **P0** |\n| Missing timeout cleanup | 🔴 Critical | Stale state | Low | **P0** |\n| Motion variants recreation | 🟡 Medium | Allocations | Low | P1 |\n| Missing React.memo | 🟡 Medium | Re-renders | Medium | P1 |\n| Redundant parsing | 🟡 Medium | O(n) waste | Low | P1 |\n| Socket listener leak | 🟡 Medium | Duplicates | Low | P2 |\n| No request cache | 🟢 Nice | Server load | Medium | P3 |\n| No virtualization | 🟢 Nice | Large lists | High | P3 |\n| No search debounce | 🟢 Nice | Input lag | Low | P3 |\n\n**Recommended order:** Fix all 🔴 Critical issues first (P0), then 🟡 Medium (P1-P2), then 🟢 Nice-to-have (P3).\n",
